description = "Ikemen GO, the open source M.U.G.E.N-compatible fighting game engine. Load the folder of an Ikemen GO installation, or any file inside it (data/system.def works), and the engine runs from there. Configuration, saves, replays and screenshots stay in that folder's save/ directory."
notes = "The core renders on its own, outside the frontend's context. The default build opens a hidden desktop-GL window, so it needs a display server (or SDL's offscreen video driver). The IKEMEN_GLES=1 build instead renders GL ES 3.0 into a windowless EGL pbuffer, which is what a KMS/DRM frontend needs since it already holds the DRM master. Player 1-4 map to RetroPad ports 1-4; the keyboard is forwarded as well, so the engine's own input configuration screens work."
